    "id": "p32-q71-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "71",
    "prompt": "Complete the square of the following by adding the $2ab$ term.\n$$4a^2+9$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(2a+3)^2-12a$ or $(2a-3)^2+12a$.",
      "worked": "The middle term is $2(2a)(3)=12a$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4a^2+9&=4a^2+12a+9-12a\\\\4a^2+9&=(2a+3)^2-12a.\\end{align*}$$\nAlternatively:\n$$\\begin{align*}4a^2+9&=4a^2-12a+9+12a\\\\4a^2+9&=(2a-3)^2+12a.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 18
  },
